Day 239/250: Maximum Side Length of a Square with a Sum Less than or Equal to Threshold

Problem Statement #1292

Problem Statement Explanation:

Given a m x n matrix mat and an integer threshold, return the maximum side-length of a square with a sum less than or equal to threshold or return 0 if no such square exists.

Solution Approach:


The challenge in this problem is to efficiently calculate the sum of any square sub-matrix and find the largest one that fits within the threshold. We use two primary techniques:

1. 2D Prefix Sum
To avoid re-calculating the sum of sub-matrices repeatedly, we pre-compute a 2D Prefix Sum array.
prefixSum[i][j] stores the sum of all elements from mat[0][0] to mat[i-1][j-1].
Using the Inclusion-Exclusion Principle, the sum of any square with bottom-right corner (i,j) and side length L can be calculated in O(1) time:
Sum=P[i][j]−P[i−L][j]−P[i][j−L]+P[i−L][j−L]

2. Greedy Sliding Window (Optimization)
Instead of using Binary Search to find the side length (which would be O(MNlog(min(M,N)))), we can optimize to O(MN):
We iterate through every cell (i,j) in the matrix.
We only check if a square of size (currentMaxSide + 1) can be formed ending at the current cell.
If the sum of this larger square is ≤ threshold, we increment our currentMaxSide.
Since we only care about the maximum length, we don't need to check smaller squares once a larger one is found.

Here's the code:

class Solution {
    public int maxSideLength(int[][] mat, int threshold) {
        int m = mat.length;
        int n = mat[0].length;
        int[][] prefixSum = new int[m + 1][n + 1];

        for (int i = 1; i <= m; i++) {
            for (int j = 1; j <= n; j++) {
                prefixSum[i][j] = mat[i-1][j-1] + prefixSum[i-1][j] + 
                                  prefixSum[i][j-1] - prefixSum[i-1][j-1];
            }
        }
        
        int maxSide = 0;
        for (int i = 1; i <= m; i++) {
            for (int j = 1; j <= n; j++) {
                int nextSide = maxSide + 1;
                if (i >= nextSide && j >= nextSide) {
                    int currentSum = prefixSum[i][j] 
                                   - prefixSum[i - nextSide][j] 
                                   - prefixSum[i][j - nextSide] 
                                   + prefixSum[i - nextSide][j - nextSide];
                    
                    if (currentSum <= threshold) {
                        maxSide = nextSide;
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        
        return maxSide;
    }
}

Complexity:

Time Complexity: O(M×N)
Space Complexity: O(M×N)




